- **$m = 0$:** $x^2 > 0 \\implies x \\neq 0$، إذن $D_{f_0} = \\mathbb{R}^*$.

- **$m < 0$:** $x^2 > -m = |m| \\implies |x| > \\sqrt{|m|}$، إذن $D_{f_m} = \\;]-\\infty, -\\sqrt{|m|}[ \\,\\cup\\, ]\\sqrt{|m|}, +\\infty[$.

**الخلاصة:**
- $m > 0$: $D = \\mathbb{R}$
- $m = 0$: $D = \\mathbb{R}^*$
- $m < 0$: $D = \\mathbb{R} \\setminus [-\\sqrt{|m|}, \\sqrt{|m|}]$
`,
    methodology:
